DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The llllddppdd daemon receives Link Layer Discovery Protocol (LLDP) messages
     on Ethernet interfaces and stores them for display by lldp(8).

     LLDP is a link layer protocol for advertising and discovering identity
     and capability.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd          Do not daemonize.  If this option is specified, llllddppdd will
                 run in the foreground and log to stderr.

     --ss _s_o_c_k_e_t   Use _s_o_c_k_e_t to communicate with lldp(8).

